      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I am not sure what you mean as for weird blue tint, but specular highlights is part of a PBR shader's BDRF, so it is PBR. Reflection probes are IBS or Image Based Shading. And these are not cheap to render on android. Tho i'll trust that the new processor can render them better as you said.\n\nAlso ramp lit is not \"just\", it requires various additional calculations to make sure the spherical harmonics are averaged to sample the ramp.\n\nBut i can't say a lot, i saw the code for the toon lit shader and they could've just took the w of the first spherical harmonics instead of sampling it 7 times. \n\nI doubt that they'll add transparency tho, it's still something very heavy and it'd be heavy enough is someone used it on their quest world.\n\nFor ambient occlusion it'd be cool to have it, for now it's good with having a duplicate of the main texture multiplied by the ao.\n\nFor now the only extra thing you can do with your materials is, using standard lite, disable specular highlights, setting the smoothness to 0, disable the normals in the model, then you'll be able to have a flat shaded material with support for emission, at the cost that BRDF and other PBR functions will appear wrongly. I hope more shaders or shader options get added soon.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-11-18T20:12:47.569Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "The current quest shaders are extremely outdated and were made for the quest 1, which itself is pretty outdated, and I think are too limiting for most avatars, I'm not asking for custom shaders, just some extra shaders that would allow for some more customization, gonna give a few examples\nExample 1: Matcap PBR - Like standard lite but using a matcap for reflections instead of the weird blue thing it uses that doesn't actually use reflection probes for whatever reason (Snapdragon XR2 can handle those IIRC)\nExample 2: Ramp Lit - Literally a shader that's lit by a light ramp, would effectively be a lightweight toon shader.\nExample 3: Bumped Matcap - Literally just the matcap shader but with normal map support\nExample 4: Bumped Specular Reflective - Same as bumped specular but with support for a cubemap or matcap to be used for reflections, preferrably with a mask.\nExample 5: Additive Matcap - Same as Matcap but Additive blending instead of multiplicative\nExample 6?: not sure if this is possible, but possibly allow for a form of transparency that doesn't introduce large amounts of overdraw by limiting the amount of times it can render be exactly once, this would cause visual artifacting when multiple transparent surfaces overlap as they'd dissapear behind eachother, but that's better than no transparency or the performance impact of having multiple surfaces overdraw.\nAs for the current shaders, I feel like a few improvements could be the specular shaders being given fake specular highlights with baked lighting (like poiyomi has), Standard lite using the world's reflection probes instead of that weird blue tint that it has (that's not how PBR works, could even be a simplified implementation where it doesn't support box projection), also having AO support.",
